{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Therefore, upon them.</b> Upon the people of Judah who were conspiring against Ahaz." "<b>Its channels.</b> Strong places of water, like עַל אֲפִיקֵי מַיִם (Psalms 12:6) — or according to the interpretation of the place [i.e., the plain sense, that אפיקים means river channels]." "And likewise <b>its banks.</b> Some say it is missing a resh, like שַׁרְשְׁרֹת with שְׁרָשֹׁת (Exodus 28:14, 22), but they have said nothing, for the resh is doubled and is not a root letter, for the root of שַׁרְשְׁרוֹת is שׁרשׁ, but a missing resh would not be found, for it is not one of the root letters."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {2 "Ibn Ezra's argument is compressed: those who say גדות is defective for שרשות are wrong, because in שרשרות the resh is a doubled non-root letter, so its absence from גדות proves גדות is a different word entirely, not a defective form."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:49.968187567Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}